 "as_found": "grip.core is the pressed core from the moment the mould opens (SEAM.md section 10). Its as-found set (tex/grip__dirty_*) is the core fresh from the mould: dull grey skin under release powder, pocket and holes as cast, a dark witness line on the parting plane. Three wipes on the core: skin (the whole core), flash (the slab round the parting plane, Y = 0) and pocket. The zones overlap: a texel should show the clean set only when EVERY zone that holds it has been wiped, so the pocket and the parting line stay as cast until s4.flash even if the skin is cleaned first. The seams' as-found state is the uncured paste. The two spring clips in the loop channel are part of the core mesh and are there in both sets"
